Summary of changes made in this fork
------------------------------------
- Rebranded the application from "Homarr" to "iFrame" (name, logo, icons,
  colours, metadata) while retaining the upstream credit above.
- Added "iFrame pages": embedding a web page as a titled, collapsible board
  section.
- Added a login-capable reverse proxy for embedded pages (serving a site under
  the panel's own origin so its session cookie is first-party), with an
  optional dedicated-origin mode gated by a signed token (EMBED_PROXY_ORIGIN).
- Added self-contained widgets (including a sports ticker and a Discord widget)
  and quick-add presets for popular chat apps.
- Scoped the widget picker to self-contained "web" widgets and removed the
  external-integrations surface from the UI.
- Removed the upstream update-checker UI and release-notice checks.
- Removed Homarr-specific project tooling (CI workflows, issue templates, etc.).

